---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";

const guides = [
  {
    href: "/docs/installation",
    title: "Installation",
    detail: "Set up the host, dispatcher core, trusted registry, admin panel, and Jenkins.",
    icon: "wrench-screwdriver",
  },
  {
    href: "/docs/triggers",
    title: "Triggers & ingest",
    detail: "Point Jira, GitHub, or Linear at the ingest endpoint and forward to Jenkins.",
    icon: "bolt",
  },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Documentation"
  description="Install fleet and configure triggers: the admin ingest endpoint, forwarding to Jenkins, and PM-source webhooks."
>
  <div class="docs-prose">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-primary/80">documentation</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-base-content sm:text-4xl">
      fleet documentation
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg">
      How to install the dispatcher and panel, and how tasks enter the system — from a PM tool
      webhook, through the panel's ingest endpoint, and on to the Jenkins Generic Webhook Trigger.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {
      guides.map((guide) => (
        <a
          href={guide.href}
          data-astro-prefetch
          class="group rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-content/[0.02] p-6 transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:border-primary/30 hover:bg-base-content/[0.04]"
        >
          <div class="mb-4 inline-grid size-11 place-items-center rounded-xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-content/5 text-primary">
            <Icon name={guide.icon} class="size-5" />
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-base-content">{guide.title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">{guide.detail}</p>
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="docs-prose mt-10">
    <h2>What lives where</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a data-astro-prefetch href="/docs/installation">Installation</a> — toolchain, <code>fleetctl</code>, registry
        overlay, admin panel, and the Jenkins job.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a data-astro-prefetch href="/docs/triggers">Triggers &amp; ingest</a> — the <code>POST /api/ingest</code>{" "}
        endpoint (record + forward), authentication, the <code>x-fleet-*</code> headers, and the
        Jenkins Generic Webhook Trigger wiring.
      </li>
      <li>
        Deeper references are kept alongside the code in{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/wrbl606/fleet/tree/main/docs">docs/</a> — contract, runner
        backends, security model, host hardening, and scale/observability.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Ingest in one paragraph</h2>
    <p>
      External senders POST to the admin panel's <code>/api/ingest?source=&lt;source&gt;</code>{" "}
      endpoint. The panel records the event as <code>webhook.received</code> in the run ledger and
      forwards the raw body verbatim to the configured dispatcher (<code>FLEET_WEBHOOK_URL</code>,
      normally the Jenkins Generic Webhook Trigger). Without a <code>source</code>, the same
      endpoint is a ledger sink for the dispatcher's own lifecycle events and never forwards. See{" "}
      <a data-astro-prefetch href="/docs/triggers">Triggers &amp; ingest</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
